#. type: Title ==
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mechanical Crafting"
msgstr "动力合成"

#. type: #crafting
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:117
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "When the ingredients and output match a mechanical crafting recipe, a "
#| "\"use mechanical crafting\" button (<<figure-crafting-1>> ❶) is revealed. "
#| "With this option toggled on, when packages created by this gauge are "
#| "unpacked onto mechanical crafters, the ingredients are automatically "
#| "arranged into the crafting pattern (❷)."
msgid ""
"When the configured recipe in a factory gauge matches the item types of a "
"mechanical crafting recipe, a \"use mechanical crafting\" button (<<figure-"
"crafting-1>> ❶) is revealed. With this option toggled on, when packages "
"created by this gauge are unpacked onto mechanical crafters, the ingredients "
"are automatically arranged into the crafting pattern (❷)."
msgstr ""
"当原材料和产物与一条动力合成配方相符时，界面会出现“使用动力合成”按钮"
"（<<figure-crafting-1>> ❶）。启用后，仪表生成的包裹在动力合成器上解包时，原材"
"料会自动按照 ❷ 显示的配方布局排列。"

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crafting 1 iron sword"
msgstr "合成 1 把铁剑"

#. type: #figure-crafting-1
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:123
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The crafting recipe may be at most 10×10 in size. However, when it is "
#| "larger than 3×3, ❷ no longer previews the pattern, and factory gauges "
#| "that ignore NBT data may not be used as ingredients."
msgid ""
"The crafting recipe may be at most 10×10 in size. However, when it is larger "
"than 3×3, ❷ no longer previews the pattern. Instead, hold ctrl while "
"hovering to reveal a preview tooltip. Factory gauges that ignore NBT data "
"may not be used as ingredients for crafting recipes larger than 3×3. If the "
"ingredients of a large crafting recipe cannot be packed within 9 stacks, ❶ "
"is not shown."
msgstr ""
"动力合成配方最大可为 10×10。配方大于 3×3 时，❷ 不再预览具体布局。忽略 NBT 数"
"据的工厂仪表不能作为此类配方的原材料。"

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crafting crushing wheels"
msgstr "合成粉碎轮"

#. type: #figure-crafting-1
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:128
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The mechanical crafters must be connected using a wrench and arranged in "
#| "a square grid between 3×3 and 10×10 in size. Smaller recipes may be sent "
#| "to larger mechanical crafter arrangements. Hold Ctrl and scroll on the "
#| "ingredients to adjust the crafting grid size to match the crafter "
#| "arrangement they will be sent to."
msgid ""
"The mechanical crafters must be connected using a wrench and arranged in a "
"square grid between 3×3 and 10×10 in size. Smaller recipes may be sent to "
"larger mechanical crafter arrangements. Hold ctrl and scroll on the "
"ingredients to adjust the crafting grid size to match the crafter "
"arrangement they will be sent to."
msgstr ""
"动力合成器必须使用扳手互相连接，并排列为 3×3 至 10×10 的正方形网格。较小配方"
"可以发送到更大的动力合成器阵列：按住 Ctrl 并在原材料上滚动，可调整合成网格大"
"小，使其与目标合成器大小相同。"

#. type: #figure-crafting-1
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:130
msgid ""
"It is recommended to use a repackager before unpacking onto mechanical "
"crafters, see the in-game ponder on repackagers."
msgstr "建议在动力合成器前使用理包机，参阅游戏内关于理包机的“思索”。"

#. type: Title ===
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch Crafting"
msgstr "批量合成"

#. type: #batch-crafting
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:135
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "A factory gauge may be configured to send ingredients enough to craft "
#| "multiple output items at once. When mechanical crafting is turned on, "
#| "scroll on the output slot (<<figure-crafting-batch>> ❶) to adjust how "
#| "many items to craft each batch. The number of ingredients (❷) are matched "
#| "automatically and cannot be adjusted individually."
msgid ""
"A factory gauge may be configured with a <<term-recipe,recipe>> whose "
"amounts are multiples of a crafting recipe. With mechanical crafting turned "
"on, scroll on an ingredient or output slot (<<figure-crafting-batch>> ❶❷) to "
"adjust the [#term-batch-size]_batch size_, which is the number of times "
"crafting can be performed as a part of this recipe. The number of "
"ingredients (❷) and output (❶) are calculated automatically and cannot be "
"adjusted individually."
msgstr ""
"工厂仪表可以一次发送足够进行多次合成的原材料。启用动力合成后，在产物槽"
"（<<figure-crafting-batch>> ❶）上滚动可调整每批需要合成的产物数量。原材料数量"
"（❷）会自动匹配，不能逐项调整。"

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crafting iron swords in 64-item batches"
msgstr "每批合成 64 把铁剑"

#. type: #figure-crafting-batch
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:141
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Using a repackager is mandatory when batch crafting is used. When a "
#| "repackager receives a package containing ingredients for multiple crafts, "
#| "it is repackaged into multiple smaller packages containing ingredients "
#| "for 1 craft each, which may then be unpacked onto mechanical crafters."
msgid ""
"Using a repackager is mandatory when batch crafting is used. When a "
"repackager receives all packages created from a <<term-request,request>>, "
"the contents are repackaged into multiple smaller packages, each containing "
"ingredients to craft one time, which may then be unpacked onto mechanical "
"crafters."
msgstr ""
"使用批量合成时，必须使用理包机。理包机会把包含多次合成原材料的大包裹重新拆分"
"成多个小包裹，每个小包裹只包含一次合成所需的原材料，才可以解包到动力合成器"
"上。"

#. type: #figure-crafting-batch
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:143
msgid ""
"The maximum batch size is 64, regardless of the stack size of the output "
"item. The maximum number of output items is consequently 64 × the number of "
"outputs in the crafting recipe."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:144
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crafting crushing wheels in batches of 64, producing 128 items per batch"
msgstr ""

#. type: #figure-crafting-batch
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:148
msgid ""
"When using batch crafting, the total number of ingredients in a recipe may "
"exceed 9 stacks, in which case the ingredients are split into multiple "
"packages. This is allowed because the repackager outputs only packages "
"containing ingredients to craft one time, not the entire recipe."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify Ingredient Arrangement"
msgstr ""

#. type: #ingredient-arrange
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:153
msgid ""
"By default, when packages created by factory gauges are unpacked, the "
"contents are not arranged in any specific order. Clicking <<figure-arrange-"
"deployer>> ❶ enables custom arrangement, allowing the <<term-recipe,recipe>> "
"to assign each ingredient to any of the 9 slots. This is similar to "
"<<crafting,mechanical crafting>>, but the arrangements may be arbitrary, and "
"are not limited to crafting recipes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using a custom arrangement to represent a deploying recipe"
msgstr ""

#. type: #figure-arrange-deployer
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:159
msgid ""
"When custom arrangement is enabled, each ingredient in the recipe (❷) may be "
"dragged with the left mouse button to be moved to another slot, or dragged "
"with the right mouse button to be duplicated. The number of each duplicated "
"item stack of one ingredient can be adjusted independently."
msgstr ""

#. type: #figure-arrange-deployer
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:161
msgid ""
"Using a repackager is required for the custom arrangement to take effect, "
"even if one package already contains all the ingredients of a recipe. The "
"ingredients are repackaged into one package, which can then be unpacked into "
"any container block. Ingredients are unpacked into their assigned slot(s). "
"In the example given by <<figure-arrange-deployer>>, the sandpapers are "
"unpacked into the 1st-3rd slots of the container, and the rose quartz are "
"unpack into the 9th slot. The receiving end may then be set up to transfer "
"the items in the 1st-3rd slots onto a deployer, and the items in the 9th "
"slot under the deployer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:162
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contents of a package created by <<figure-arrange-deployer>> unpacked into an empty chest"
msgstr ""

#. type: #figure-arrange-deployer
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:166
msgid ""
"For unpacking to be possible, each item stack specified in ❷ must be "
"unpacked into each of the first 9 slots of the target container. It may "
"stack with existing items in the slot, if they are stackable and do not "
"exceed the stack size. Item stacks do not overflow to another slot. The "
"target container may have fewer than 9 slots, if the custom arrangement does "
"not make use of the slots beyond what is available in the container."
msgstr ""

#. type: #figure-arrange-deployer
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:168
msgid ""
"A package with custom arrangement may be unpacked into any block supported "
"by packagers. The contents are unpacked according to the number and order of "
"slots made available by the target block. For example, such packages may be "
"unpacked directly onto a vanilla crafter to perform batch crafting; but a "
"package containing both a smeltable item and a fuel may not be unpacked onto "
"a furnace, because a packager may only access one of the slots in the "
"furnace depending on the side it is attached to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:170
